version 3.6.0
- Add the InjectApi interface and InjectAgentBase with a Python inject_client, exposing a unified inject API to the inject agent.
- Add adb connection management: adb server / endpoint probing, device listing, a connection coordinator with cooldown, failure quarantine and recovery probing, plus connection metrics and a health snapshot.
- Rework the native logger: bounded queue, batched disk writes, daily rolling with retention, and dropped / IO-error reporting.
- Add thread hook utilities: ThreadDumper, and hooks for the thread pool executor and uncaught throwables.
- Add inject flags and path redirection to the inject agent; make destroy idempotent and register it with atexit.
- Kill the whole process group when a shell command times out.

version 3.5.0
- Add class hook APIs: hook_class / unhook_class with static, instance and constructor scope, and a safe tostring option.
- Add native library monitoring APIs: get modules / functions, watch function, watch library load, dump native method and the onLibLoad callback.
- Add read_file / read_maps / read_smaps and set_to_string_config for configuring the SafeToString output.
- Add dump_all_threads for dumping all java threads of the target app.
- System server: add stability_test, clear_uid, set_intercept_all and set_app_android_id.
- Add mount / umount, launch mount / umount and hide_path; add set_dex_load_timeout.
- Send app package name and version when adding rules automatically; add set_app_info / get_app_info.
- Save crash logs to local files when the app process crashes.
- Optimize the interception of system applications: support Android 13+ PidMap and registerReceiver hooks, and the Xiaomi attachApplicationLocked variant.
- Report the specific failure reason (dex load result) when loading a plugin.

version 3.4.0
- Add the API for granting permissions.
- Optimize the interception of system applications.
- Instruction hook support trace return.
- Optimize the support for wireless devices.

version 3.3.0
- Rpc call improve
- Optimize the hook for inline methods

version 3.2.0
 - The plugin adds callback methods beforeNewApplication and afterNewApplication
 - Optimize the hook of the method instructions to implement the callbacks of the plugin-related methods before and after the creation of the application
 - Add an example of a plugin rpc call
 - Support obtaining configuration files by reading environment variables
 - When registering a plugin, send the app package name and version information also

version 3.1.0
 - Optimize the sending of messages, add support for saving logs and redirecting app logs
 - rpc adds parsing for long strings. Add a callback for successful injection into the app
 - Optimize the test code and add exception catching

version 2.1.0
 - Anti detection by remove the writable executable  memory fragments.

version 2.0.2:
 - rpc improve.
 - Add annotations to the rpc method.
 - AlbatrossServerApi is added.

version 2.0.1:
 - Support monitoring local changes in the plugin. If recompiled, re-inject.
 - optimize attach by obtain all java processes of the app based on uid.
 - Optimize the management of plugins, state switching, and method callbacks.
 - A series of plugin-related apis have been added.

version 2.0.0:
 - Clean api is added.
 - Add plugins to add, delete and modify apis.
 - Support for system plugins.
 - Add a new injection mode launch fast for faster speed.

version 1.0.2:
 - Java rpc call improve.

version 1.0.1:
 - Compatible with window system.
 - Do not disable Selinux default.

version 1.0.0:
 - Initial version.